The OpenState engine (the openstate-engine binary, the "Engine") is
proprietary. It is licensed, not sold. These terms are also published at
https://michael-a-kuykendall.github.io/openstate/terms.html

1. Grant. Anyone may install and use the Engine free of charge; on each
   machine the first 30 structural applies are free. With a paid license
   (a monthly subscription, or lifetime), you (one named developer) may use
   the Engine without that limit on up to 3 machines at a time, for personal
   or commercial work: every 0.x release for a lifetime license, and while
   the subscription is paid for a monthly one. The license is personal: it
   does not transfer to another person. A team buys one license per
   developer. A monthly license may be switched to lifetime by paying the
   lifetime price; the key stays the same and the unused part of the
   current month is not credited.

2. Restrictions. You may not redistribute, sublicense, sell or rent the
   Engine, embed it in another product or hosted service, or reverse engineer
   it except where applicable law allows this despite this restriction. A
   commercial license for embedding is available from
   michaelallenkuykendall@gmail.com.

3. License checks. The Engine checks licenses over the network with Keygen
   and the OpenState license worker: on the free tier each structural apply
   is counted, and a paid license is verified and may be used offline for up
   to 7 days between checks. It sends the license key, a hashed machine
   fingerprint and the platform name, never project data. Circumventing the
   check is not permitted by these terms.

4. No refunds. All sales are final (see
   https://michael-a-kuykendall.github.io/openstate/refund.html). If you are an
   EU consumer, you waived the statutory 14-day right of withdrawal by
   requesting immediate access to the license at checkout.

5. Public components. The documentation, skill (SKILL.md), installer
   (install.sh) and plugin bundle are licensed under the MIT License (see
   PUBLIC-LICENSE), not under these terms.

